---
import PageTitle from '../components/PageTitle.astro';
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';

const description = 'What this site is for.';
---

<Base title="About" description={description}>
	<PageTitle kicker="About" title="About this site" />
	<div class="prose">
		<p>
			This is a working record of the control system I'm building for my model railway, and of
			<a href="/projects/westgate-hollow/">Westgate Hollow Yard</a>, the small OO gauge test layout it's being proven
			on. It's written mainly for me: what I did, when, and why I made each decision.
		</p>
		<p>
			Westgate Hollow is a stepping stone. It exists to verify the control system, to try out scenic techniques, and
			for general practice before I build a larger full-room layout.
		</p>
		<p>
			The <a href="/log/">log</a> tracks progress. The <a href="/projects/">projects</a> pages describe each part of the
			system. The <a href="/decisions/">decisions</a> record the design choices and the reasoning behind them.
		</p>
	</div>
</Base>
